<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                           revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Lärarrummet (teacher app)</displayName>
  <description>Settings that school IT locks for Lärarrummet.</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_0_10">Lärarrummet 0.10.0 or later</string>
      <string id="Laxspelet">Lärarrummet</string>
      <string id="MaxNiva">Highest permission level</string>
      <string id="MaxNiva_Help">The highest level teachers on this computer can get, regardless of the principal's decision in the app.

Level 0: no personal data about pupils. Newsletters, study material, class team and class insight (totals only, at least 5 families). Families are shown as "Familj 1, 2, 3 ...".
Level 1: as level 0, plus pupils' names, groups and timetables.
Level 2: as level 1, plus data about individual pupils that guardians choose to share (reports, statistics, notes, test results).

When the level is lowered, the app immediately deletes copies of pupil data that are no longer allowed.
If the policy is set for both computer and user, the lowest level applies.

Recommended: level 0 until the data protection officer has made an assessment.
More (Swedish): https://github.com/lolander/Skolan/blob/main/docs/larare-skolor.md</string>
      <string id="Niva0">Level 0: no personal data (recommended)</string>
      <string id="Niva1">Level 1: pupil names</string>
      <string id="Niva2">Level 2: data about individual pupils</string>
      <string id="Uppdateringar">Updates</string>
      <string id="Uppdateringar_Help">How Lärarrummet is updated.

Automatic: the app downloads new versions from the project's GitHub page and installs them silently when not in use. Files are only installed if their SHA-256 fingerprint matches.
Ask: the teacher sees that a new version exists and installs it.
Off: the app never contacts GitHub. IT distributes new versions.

Installations for all users (/ALLUSERS) or from Microsoft Store never update themselves.</string>
      <string id="Automatisk">Automatic</string>
      <string id="Manuell">Ask the teacher</string>
      <string id="Av">Off (IT distributes)</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="MaxNiva">
        <dropdownList refId="MaxNiva" noSort="true" defaultItem="0">Highest level:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Uppdateringar">
        <dropdownList refId="Uppdateringar" noSort="true" defaultItem="2">Updates:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
